Pope Francis has promised to take action  on child abusers in the Catholic Church  only weeks ago it was revealed that  nearly 400 priests had been dismissed in  the last two years because of suspected  molestation of children but church  policy is to investigate the allegations  internally at the UN Committee says  that's not good enough another matter  was the code of silence that was imposed  by the church on children and the fact  that reporting to national law  enforcement authorities has never been  made compulsory the UN report estimates  the number of victims in the tens of  thousands it says the church has failed  children the main finding of the  committee was that the Holy See has  adopted policies and practices which  have led to the continuation of the  abuse by and the impunity of the  perpetrators the Holy See has  consistently placed the preservation of  the reputation of the church and the  protection of the perpetrators above  children's best interests the committee  also criticized the Church's position on  homosexuality contraception and abortion  it's calling for an overhaul of vatican  policy
 

